    .header{padding:.8rem 1rem}
    .section{padding:2rem 1rem}
    .card{padding:1.5rem}
  }

  /* ── Fade-in animation ── */
  .card{opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px);transition:opacity .6s ease,transform .6s ease}
  .card.visible{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ── Header ── -->
<header class="header">
  <h1>☁️ Why Is the Sky Blue? / 天空为什么是蓝色的？</h1>
  <div class="lang-toggle">
    <button class="active" onclick="showLang('both')">Both 双语</button>
    <button onclick="showLang('en')">English</button>
    <button onclick="showLang('zh')">中文</button>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ── Nav Dots ── -->
<nav class="nav-dots" id="navDots">
  <a href="#hero" title="Home" class="active"></a>
  <a href="#toddler" title="Toddler"></a>
  <a href="#teenager" title="Teenager"></a>
  <a href="#phd" title="PhD"></a>
</nav>

<!-- ── Presentation ── -->
<main class="presentation">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section hero" id="hero">
    <div>
      <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">天空为什么是蓝色的？ — A Bilingual Explanation</p>
      <div class="divider"><span>Scroll to explore ↓</span></div>
      <p class="scroll-hint">▼</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Toddler -->
  <section class="section" id="toddler">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="card en-card">
        <div class="badge en">🇬🇧 English</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🧒</span>For a 3-Year-Old</h2>
        <p>The sky looks blue because sunlight is made of lots of colors mixed together — like a rainbow! When sunlight comes into our air, the blue color bounces around the most. It spreads everywhere in the sky, so when we look up, our eyes see all that blue light. That's why the sky is blue!</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card zh-card">
        <div class="badge zh">🇨🇳 中文</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🧒</span>给三岁的小朋友听</h2>
        <p>天空看起来是蓝色的，因为阳光是由很多颜色混合在一起的——就像彩虹一样！当阳光照进我们周围的空气时，蓝色会最多地弹来弹去。它遍布整个天空，所以我们抬头看的时候，眼睛看到的全是蓝色的光。这就是天空是蓝色的原因啦！</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Teenager -->
  <section class="section" id="teenager">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="card en-card">
        <div class="badge en">🇬🇧 English</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🎒</span>For a High School Teenager</h2>
        <p>The sky is blue because of something called <strong style="color:var(--accent-blue)">Rayleigh scattering</strong>. Sunlight might look white, but it's actually made up of all the colors of the rainbow (red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet). Each color travels as a wave, and blue and violet light have shorter, tighter waves compared to red light.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen). These molecules are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light, so they scatter the shorter-wavelength light (blue and violet) much more strongly than the longer-wavelength light (red, orange, yellow). This is described by Rayleigh's law:</p>
        <div class="formula">I ∝ 1/λ⁴</div>
        <p>So blue light (~450 nm) gets scattered about 10× more than red light (~650 nm).</p>
        <div class="highlight-box">
          <p>🤔 But wait — if violet has an even shorter wavelength, why isn't the sky violet?</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The sun emits much more blue light than violet light.</li>
            <li>Our eyes are more sensitive to blue than violet.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card zh-card">
        <div class="badge zh">🇨🇳 中文</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🎒</span>给高中生听</h2>
        <p>天空是蓝色的，这是因为一种叫做<strong style="color:var(--accent-purple)">瑞利散射</strong>的现象。阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它由彩虹的所有颜色组成（红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、靛、紫）。每种颜色都以波的形式传播，与红光相比，蓝光和紫光的波长更短、更紧密。</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会与气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）发生碰撞。这些分子比可见光的波长小得多，因此它们对短波长光（蓝色和紫色）的散射作用远强于对长波长光（红色、橙色、黄色）的散射。这可以用瑞利定律来描述：</p>
        <div class="formula">I ∝ 1/λ⁴</div>
        <p>因此，蓝光（约 450 纳米）的散射量大约是红光（约 650 纳米）的 10 倍。</p>
        <div class="highlight-box">
          <p>🤔 但是等一下——如果紫光的波长更短，为什么天空不是紫色的呢？</p>
          <ul>
            <li>太阳发出的蓝光比紫光多得多。</li>
            <li>我们的眼睛对蓝色的敏感度高于紫色。</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PhD -->
  <section class="section" id="phd">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="card en-card" style="grid-column:1/-1">
        <div class="badge en">🇬🇧 English</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🔬</span>For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <p>The blue color of the daytime sky arises from <strong style="color:var(--accent-blue)">elastic scattering of solar radiation by atmospheric molecules</strong> — a phenomenon quantitatively described by <strong style="color:var(--accent-blue)">Rayleigh scattering theory</strong>.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">Consider an incident electromagnetic wave (solar radiation) with wavevector <strong style="color:var(--accent-cyan)">k⃗ᵢ</strong> and frequency ω interacting with a bound electron in an atmospheric molecule (predominantly N₂ and O₂). In the dipole approximation — valid when particle size a ≪ λ — the oscillating electric field <strong style="color:var(--accent-cyan)">E⃗</strong> induces an oscillating dipole moment:</p>
        <div class="formula">p⃗(t) = α E⃗(t)</div>
        <p>where α is the molecular polarizability tensor. The induced dipole radiates as a classical oscillating dipole, with a differential scattering cross-section given by:</p>
        <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (k⁴|α|² / 16π²ε₀²) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>where k = 2π/λ is the wavenumber and θ is the scattering angle. The crucial dependence is the <strong style="color:var(--accent-cyan)">k⁴ (or λ⁻⁴) scaling</strong>, meaning shorter wavelengths scatter dramatically more intensely.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">For randomly oriented molecules, the total scattering cross-section per molecule is:</p>
        <div class="formula">σ = 8π³α² / (3λ⁴)</div>
        <p>The intensity of scattered light at path length L follows:</p>
        <div class="formula">I(λ) = I₀(λ) · n · σ(λ) · L = I₀(λ) · C/λ⁴</div>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">The <strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">perceived</strong> color results from folding this spectral dependence with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Solar spectral irradiance</strong> E⊙(λ) (~5778 K blackbody), peaking near 500 nm.</li>
          <li><strong>Atmospheric transmission</strong> T(λ), accounting for absorption (e.g., ozone Chappuis band).</li>
          <li><strong>CIE color matching functions</strong> x̄(λ), ȳ(λ), z̄(λ), modeling human cone response.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">The tristimulus values are:</p>
        <div class="formula">X = ∫ E⊙(λ) · T(λ) · (1/λ⁴) · x̄(λ) dλ</div>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">The λ⁻⁴ dependence overwhelmingly favors blue, but integration yields a <strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">desaturated blue</strong> — not spectral violet — because:</p>
        <ol style="padding-left:1.5rem;margin-top:.5rem">
          <li>The solar spectrum drops off in the UV/violet (Planck distribution at ~5778 K).</li>
          <li>The human V(λ) luminosity function and cone sensitivities fall off sharply below ~420 nm.</li>
          <li>Multiple scattering and aerosol (Mie) contributions add a broadband white component, further desaturating the hue.</li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">At larger zenith angles, the increased path length amplifies the λ⁻⁴ effect for transmitted light, preferentially removing blue and leaving the red/orange spectrum at sunrise and sunset — a beautiful confirmation of the same scattering physics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card zh-card" style="grid-column:1/-1">
        <div class="badge zh">🇨🇳 中文</div>
        <h2><span class="emoji">🔬</span>给物理学博士听</h2>
        <p>白天天空的蓝色来源于<strong style="color:var(--accent-purple)">太阳辐射被大气分子弹性散射</strong>——这一现象可以用<strong style="color:var(--accent-purple)">瑞利散射理论</strong>进行定量描述。</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">考虑一个波矢为 <strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">k⃗ᵢ</strong>、频率为 ω 的入射电磁波（太阳辐射）与大气分子（主要为 N₂ 和 O₂）中的束缚电子发生相互作用。在偶极近似下——当粒子尺寸 a ≪ λ 时成立——振荡的电场 <strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">E⃗</strong> 会诱导出一个振荡的电偶极矩：</p>
        <div class="formula">p⃗(t) = α E⃗(t)</div>
        <p>其中 α 是分子极化率张量。诱导的电偶极子像经典振荡偶极子一样辐射，其微分散射截面为：</p>
        <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (k⁴|α|² / 16π²ε₀²) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>其中 k = 2π/λ 是波数，θ 是散射角。关键依赖关系是 <strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">k⁴（或 λ⁻⁴）标度</strong>，这意味着较短波长的光散射得强烈得多。</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">对于随机取向的分子集合，每个分子的总散射截面为：</p>
        <div class="formula">σ = 8π³α² / (3λ⁴)</div>
        <p>在大气中给定路径长度 L 处的散射光强度遵循：</p>
        <div class="formula">I(λ) = I₀(λ) · n · σ(λ) · L = I₀(λ) · C/λ⁴</div>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem"><strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">感知到的</strong>颜色源于将此光谱依赖性与以下因素折叠：</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>太阳光谱辐照度</strong> E⊙(λ)（近似为 5778 K 的黑体辐射），在约 500 纳米处达到峰值。</li>
          <li><strong>大气透射率</strong> T(λ)，考虑了吸收（如臭氧在查普伊斯波段的吸收）。</li>
          <li><strong>CIE 颜色匹配函数</strong> x̄(λ)、ȳ(λ)、z̄(λ)，用于模拟人眼锥体细胞响应。</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">三刺激值为：</p>
        <div class="formula">X = ∫ E⊙(λ) · T(λ) · (1/λ⁴) · x̄(λ) dλ</div>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">λ⁻⁴ 依赖性强烈偏向光谱的蓝色端，但积分结果得到的感知天空颜色是一种<strong style="color:var(--accent-amber)">去饱和的蓝色</strong>——而非光谱紫色——因为：</p>
        <ol style="padding-left:1.5rem;margin-top:.5rem">
          <li>太阳光谱在紫外/紫光区域下降（~5778 K 的普朗克分布）。</li>
          <li>人眼的 V(λ) 视效函数和锥体细胞灵敏度在 ~420 nm 以下急剧下降。</li>
          <li>多重散射和气溶胶（米氏散射）的贡献添加了一个宽带白色分量，进一步降低了色调的饱和度。</li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">在较大的天顶角下，增加的路径长度放大了透射光的 λ⁻⁴ 效应，优先去除蓝光，留下我们在日出和日落时观察到的红/橙光谱——这是对同一散射物理学的完美印证。</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="footer">
    <p>☁️ Why Is the Sky Blue? — A Bilingual Educational Presentation · 双语教育展示</p>
  </footer>

</main>

<script>
// ── Intersection Observer for fade-in ──
const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.card');
const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
  entries.forEach(entry => {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
      entry.target.classList.add('visible');
    }
  });
}, { threshold: 0.15 });
cards.forEach(c => observer.observe(c));

// ── Nav dot highlighting ──
const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section');
const dots = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-dots a');
const navObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
  entries.forEach(entry => {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
      const id = entry.target.id;
      dots.forEach(d => d.classList.remove('active'));
      const active = document.querySelector(`.nav-dots a[href="#${id}"]`);
      if (active) active.classList.add('active');
    }
  });
}, { threshold: 0.4 });
sections.forEach(s => navObserver.observe(s));

// ── Language toggle ──
function showLang(mode) {
  const enCards = document.querySelectorAll('.en-card');
  const zhCards = document.querySelectorAll('.zh-card');
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('.lang-toggle button');

  buttons.forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
  event.target.classList.add('active');

  if (mode === 'en') {
    enCards.forEach(c => c.style.display = '');
    zhCards.forEach(c => c.style.display = 'none');
  } else if (mode === 'zh') {
    enCards.forEach(c => c.style.display = 'none');
